 "parsed": {
  "count": 2,
  "rationale": "Deploy mfa:admin and mfa:dbadmin. Phishing always gives foothold_workstation and stolen_user. With no segmentation, pivot_internal gives reach_internal. The workstation foothold bypasses mfa_user, so the attacker can reach appserver, apiserver and ciserver. From there, kerberoast gives stolen_admin, and ciserver escalation plus leak_secrets gives stolen_dbadmin. mfa_admin blocks auth_dc and auth_adfs, so admin_dc and admin_adfs can never be reached. mfa_dbadmin then blocks auth_db, auth_fileserver and auth_backup, because the only bypass needs admin_dc or admin_adfs. No admin on db, fileserver or backup means no exfiltration. No single control works: mfa_dbadmin alone is bypassed via auth_dc, then admin_dc. mfa_admin alone falls to auth_db with stolen_dbadmin from ciserver. segmented alone falls to an escalated workstation that re-enables the pivot. mfa_user is bypassed by the phished footholds. No single patch blocks every path. So the minimum is 2."
 },
